        <briefdescription>
<para>Get the center offset between two frames at a given date. </para>
        </briefdescription>
        <detaileddescription>
<para>If the frames share the same origin, the offset is zero. If the frames share the same axis but have different origins, the offset is the relative position between the two origins in Frame_T. All calculations are done in the solar_system_barycenter::icrf frame.</para>
<para><parameterlist kind="templateparam"><parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>Frame_T</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>The first frame type. </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
<parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>Frame_U</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>The second frame type. </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
</parameterlist>
<parameterlist kind="param"><parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>date</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>The date at which to calculate the offset. </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
</parameterlist>
<simplesect kind="return"><para>CartesianVector&lt;Distance, Frame_T&gt; The offset vector from Frame_T to Frame_U expressed in Frame_T. </para>
</simplesect>
</para>
